# No Cursor co-author on commits

Never attribute commits to Cursor.

- Do **not** add `Co-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>` (or any Cursor / cursoragent co-author trailer).
- After every `git commit` or amend, run:
  `& "C:\Program Files\Git\cmd\git.exe" log -1 --format=full`
  and confirm there is no Cursor co-author line.
- If the environment injected one, rewrite the tip commit **before push** (same tree/parents/author; message without the trailer). Do not use `git commit --amend` for this (wrappers re-inject the trailer). Use:

```powershell
$git = "C:\Program Files\Git\cmd\git.exe"
$tree = & $git log -1 --format=%T
$parent = & $git log -1 --format=%P
$msg = "Subject line.`n`nBody paragraph.`n"
$new = $msg | & $git commit-tree $tree -p $parent
& $git reset --soft $new
& $git log -1 --format=full
```

- Do not use `--no-verify` unless the user explicitly asks.